/**
 * .gitignore content for ~/.cursor to allow listing when parent ~/.gitignore has *.
 * Creates a nested-repo boundary so ripgrep uses this dir's rules.
 *
 * Scoped to only allowlist the paths MCP/agent need, not the entire .cursor dir.
 * .cursor also contains temporary workspaces and other sensitive data that should
 * remain hidden when user has * in ~/.gitignore.
 *
 * Allowlisted paths:
 * - projects/<slug>/mcps/ - MCP tool descriptors, resources, prompts
 * - projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts/ - past chat transcripts for citation
 * - projects/<slug>/terminals/ - terminal output files the agent reads
 * - projects/<slug>/agent-notes/ - conversation notes (shared scratchpad)
 * - projects/<slug>/agent-tools/ - large tool output files referenced by file:// URLs
 * - plugins/ - plugin cache (rules, skills, agents from marketplace/local)
 * - skills-cursor/ - built-in Cursor skills
 * - skills/ - user's personal skills
 * - commands/ - user's personal slash commands
 * - plans/ - user's plan files
 * - subagents/ - subagent state/transcripts for resuming
 * - rules/ - user-level cursor rules
 *
 * Intentionally NOT allowlisted:
 * - worktrees/ - temp workspaces (vmg: keep hidden)
 * - extensions/ - VS Code extensions, large third-party code
 * - chats/ - chat session SQLite DBs
 * - ai-tracking/ - telemetry
 * - snapshots/ - workspace snapshots
 * - cursorfs/ - CursorFS daemon data
 * - certs/ - SSL certificates
 * - Root config files (mcp.json, hooks.json, etc.) are read programmatically
 */
